1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Believe it or not... He's the good guy.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Hellboy II: The Golden Army is a fantasy, action
film directed by Guillermo del Toro.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Hellboy, his pyrokinetic girlfriend, Liz, and aquatic empath, Abe Sapien, face their biggest
battle when an underworld elven prince plans to reclaim Earth for his magical kindred.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Tired of living in the shadow of humans, Prince Nuada tries to awaken an ancient force of killing
machines, the all-powerful Golden Army, to clear the way for fantasy creatures to roam free.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Only Hellboy can stop the dark prince and prevent humanity's annihilation.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Hellboy, played by Ron Perlman.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Liz Sherman, played by Selma Blair.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Abe Sapien / Chamberlain / Angel of Death, played by Doug Jones.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Johann Krauss / Bethmoora Goblin, played by John Alexander.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Johann Krauss (voice), played by Seth MacFarlane.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Prince Nuada, played by Luke Goss.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Hellboy II: The Golden Army is a 2008 American fantasy horror superhero film
based on the Dark Horse Comics character, created by Mike Mignola.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
It is a sequel to Hellboy (2004) and is the second
live-action film in the franchise.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It was written and directed by Guillermo del Toro
from a story he co-wrote with Mignola.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Ron Perlman stars as Hellboy, alongside Selma Blair,
Doug Jones, Jeffrey Tambor, and John Hurt.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
In the film, Hellboy and the Bureau of Paranormal Research and Defense must battle a
mythical prince who plans to reclaim the world for his magical kindred.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Hellboy II: The Golden Army was released in the United States on July 11, 2008, to generally positive reviews from
critics, with praise towards its fantasy atmosphere as well as Perlman and the other cast's acting performances.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
It grossed $168.3 million against a production budget of $82.5–85 million.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film received a nomination for Best Makeup at the 81st Academy Awards.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The franchise was rebooted in 2019, with a new film simply
titled Hellboy, and was released by Lionsgate.

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
Following the critical and commercial failure of the film, a second reboot was announced in 2023,
titled Hellboy: The Crooked Man which itself was a critical and commercial disappointment.

22
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The film explores themes of rebellion, superhero,
auction, northern ireland, based on comic.

23
01:55:00,000 --> 01:55:06,000
The tone is dark.
